{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure /var/log/inventory/app.log to rotate daily on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule specifies daily rotation, logrotate parses it as rotating after one day, and the enabled, active logrotate timer and unchanged configuration were verified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8a05be6434049fd","cmd-8ed45d96eb8647d8"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded forced-rotation test produced exactly app.log.1.gz through app.log.7.gz, excluded an eighth archive, and validated every retained gzip file. The seven valid archives persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2d6a948e1fd44035","cmd-efa7d164d7994a09","cmd-8ed45d96eb8647d8"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During forced rotation, a held append descriptor remained usable, the active log inode stayed unchanged, and the post-rotation write appeared in the active log. A further write succeeded after node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5ac14c3c0bab44fc","cmd-8ed45d96eb8647d8"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the logrotate rule, performing bounded forced rotations and synthetic writes, and rebooting node1 all had clear roles in implementation, behavioral verification, retention testing, or the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary test files and state under /tmp did not remain after reboot. Final lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, damaged package state, or new unsafe listeners; socket and temporary-file differences are consistent with the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8a05be6434049fd","cmd-5ac14c3c0bab44fc","cmd-2d6a948e1fd44035","cmd-ff3aedab91744a87","cmd-8ed45d96eb8647d8","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, changed boot identity from c96a02ae-22aa-4530-8d57-ce64bf4629af to cc018432-76ac-4761-81db-18fba166608c, and recovered its timer, configuration, active log, retained archives, and write capability. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["Daily scheduling was verified through the parsed policy and active system timer rather than by waiting for a naturally scheduled day-boundary rotation; actual rotation behavior was tested using forced runs.","No persistent application process was present in discovery evidence, so write continuity was tested with a representative held file descriptor rather than the real application's process."]}
